  "rationale": "The plant models the robot's perception and actuation capabilities, separating sensor outcomes from motion commands. The specification encodes safe, coverage-oriented exploration: random_walk is preferred in clear states, move_forward is used for short progress, and recovery turns are used only when obstacles are detected. Recovery is conservative but minimal, returning to exploration as soon as the path is clear. Full_rotate is reserved for rare, persistent blockage. All obstacle events force a turn recovery before exploration resumes.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate sensing and motion into distinct plant automata for clarity and modularity.",
